      "side": 1,
      "message": "Stopped partway through, but overall:\n\n1. If you want to assume something inside a function body, that constraint must either be encoded by the type signature of the function, or documented as a requirement of an `unsafe` function.\n2. You need to be clear on how long pointers are required to live, and who continues to own it.\n3. A pointer not being null is not sufficient to write to it.\n4. Any `unsafe` function should have a comment that says what is required to call it. If it is a public function, it should be a doc comment.",
      "revId": "4018b2f37c7dc1dc2ba099cad3ab7a9d3792cfb9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
